---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const unitMix = [
  { type: '1 BR', size: '~986 sq ft', layout: '1 bedroom, 1.5 bath' },
  { type: '2 BR standard', size: '~1,200–1,243 sq ft', layout: '2 bedroom, 2 bath' },
  { type: '2 BR top-floor', size: '1,258 sq ft', layout: 'Largest floor plan in building' },
];

const conversionHallmarks = [
  'Preservation of historic architectural details and proportions',
  'Modern systems (elevator, secure key-fob entry, fire alarm monitoring)',
  'High ceilings carried over from the original building (some units retain 11-foot ceilings)',
  'Large windows preserved on multiple exposures',
  'Individual basement storage for each unit',
];

const hoaIncludes = [
  'Water, gas, sewer, and trash',
  'Internet and telephone service',
  'Building liability insurance',
  'Property management',
  'Common-area maintenance and cleaning',
  'Fire alarm monitoring',
  'Elevator maintenance',
];
---

<Layout
  title="About the Building"
  description="History, unit mix, and features of 6 North 6th Street, a 21-unit condominium in Richmond, VA."
>
  <div class="bg-background py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="mb-8 font-serif text-4xl text-primary md:text-5xl">The Building</h1>

      <img
        alt="6 North 6th Street, exterior showing the 1914 brick masonry and 'Printers Publishers' historic ghost sign"
        class="mb-12 aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
        src={`${base}images/8dd8b7353260855ea659cf9ecddaa42el-m1650825609rd-w1280_h960_1777781486515-BBFvMr2Z.webp`}
      />

      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        6 North 6th Street is a five-story brick building constructed in 1914 in the heart of what
        is now Richmond's Financial District. After serving in commercial use for most of the
        20th century, the building was completely renovated in 2006 and converted into 21
        residential condominium units.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-3xl text-primary">Era and Context: Richmond in 1914</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        1914 was a pivotal year for Richmond. The Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond was established
        the same year — one of the original 12 Federal Reserve Banks. Richmond's downtown was a
        major commercial center for the Mid-Atlantic, with banking, tobacco, and railroad
        industries driving construction of multi-story commercial buildings. The building's
        location at 6th and Grace/Main sat at the edge of what became the city's banking and
        financial corridor.
      </p>

      <figure class="my-12">
        <img
          alt="A historic photograph of downtown Richmond's commercial core in the early 1900s, showing an ornate early-skyscraper office building with Model T automobiles parked at the curb."
          class="w-full bg-primary"
          src={`${base}images/historic_1-Cb4GWGfN.webp`}
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted-foreground italic">
          Downtown Richmond's commercial core in the early 1900s — the era in which 6 North 6th
          Street was built.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="my-12">
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-accent uppercase">
          Exterior Today
        </h3>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          <figure>
            <img
              alt="The front facade of 6 North 6th Street with awnings, the '6 North 6' wall plaque, and the street-front entrance."
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
              src={`${base}images/8dd8b7353260855ea659cf9ecddaa42el-m2025928477rd-w1280_h960_1777781486515-BWvBarVm.webp`}
            />
            <figcaption
              class="mt-3 border-t border-accent pt-2 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted-foreground italic"
            >
              Front entrance and "6 North 6" wall plaque.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img
              alt="A street-level view looking down 6th Street past the building's awnings and stone columns toward the downtown Richmond skyline."
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
              src={`${base}images/6n6_1778034429152-DgsXALRr.webp`}
            />
            <figcaption
              class="mt-3 border-t border-accent pt-2 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted-foreground italic"
            >
              Looking down 6th Street toward the downtown skyline.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <img
        alt="The lobby at 6 North 6th Street, with high ceilings, modern lighting, and a contemporary art installation"
        class="my-12 aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
        src={`${base}images/2609763_P01_1777781486515-CYC7buU8.webp`}
      />

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-primary">The 2006 Conversion</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        In 2006 the building underwent a full renovation, transforming the original
        commercial/office structure into 21 residential condominiums. Hallmarks of the conversion
        that remain today:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
        {conversionHallmarks.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-3xl text-primary">Unit Finishes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        While each unit has unique characteristics, typical finishes include hardwood floors in
        living areas, tile floors at entry and kitchen, granite countertops, stainless steel
        appliances, and custom cabinets. Many units feature recessed lighting, electric or gas
        fireplaces, walk-in closets in primary bedrooms, double vanities and soaking tubs, and
        stackable in-unit washer/dryers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-3xl text-primary">Unit Mix</h2>
      <div class="my-8 overflow-auto border border-border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-secondary/50">
            <tr class="border-b border-border">
              <th class="h-10 px-2 text-left font-semibold text-primary">Type</th>
              <th class="h-10 px-2 text-left font-semibold text-primary">Approximate Size</th>
              <th class="h-10 px-2 text-left font-semibold text-primary">Layout</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              unitMix.map((u) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-0">
                  <td class="p-2 font-medium">{u.type}</td>
                  <td class="p-2">{u.size}</td>
                  <td class="p-2">{u.layout}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-3xl text-primary">HOA Fee Includes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        The monthly HOA fee covers a generous list of services that would otherwise be paid
        separately by each unit owner:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
        {hoaIncludes.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground italic">
        Verify the current monthly fee with the management company.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 font-serif text-3xl text-primary">Pet &amp; Rental Policies</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-primary">Pets:</strong> Up to three pets (cats and dogs combined) per
          unit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-primary">Rentals:</strong> A minimum three-month rental term applies;
          short-term rentals are not permitted.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground italic">
        Always confirm with the current HOA documents.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
